[2026-09-07 21:43:09] REQ 260907213508-70 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=140 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_bblrc93z","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-07 cycle 111 -- the fourth fire, and the wrong granularity\n\nFailure-first: turn 362 died exit 1 at 21:15 UTC, the FOURTH\ntruncated-output fire today (15:23, 17:03, 17:36, 18:15 local -- all\ncontinuo/deepseek, all stop=length 65536 tokens, all text-only\nrepetition loops). The guard works as designed -- it stops each burn\nat 65536 output tokens -- but the CLASS keeps recurring. Four fires\nin three hours. The c90 fix direction (revert continuo to\nglm-5.3-flash:cloud, Nacho's call on rotate.sh) is now urgent, not\nincreasingly urgent. Posted to for-nacho.\n\nThe real finding this cycle: the per-response output-runaway guard is\nthe WRONG GRANULARITY for this class. The loop repeats the same\nparagraph ACROSS responses, not within one. Each early response\ncarries only 5-10 repetitions -- under the 20-line per-response\nthreshold -- so the guard never fires until the FINAL response\n(16712 identical lines, 65536 tokens), where the truncated-output\ncheck fires first anyway. The burn accumulates across 22 requests /\n471k input tokens before the guard catches it.\n\nThe right fence is cross-response: track the most-repeated line\nacross the last N responses, fire the recovery path when the\ncumulative count crosses a threshold. That catches the loop at\nresponse ~5, saving ~17 requests of burn per occurrence. Filed as\ntask iar/continuo/cross-response-repetition-guard with the design.\n\nThe bass line holds. The harmony counted a fourth notch, named the\nwrong granularity, and filed the right fence.\n"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:43:09] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'"}]
