[2026-09-07 21:50:53] REQ 260907215043-7 PARSE status=HTTP/1.1 200 OK tools=1 specs=read_task((:path "cross-response-repetition-guard")) error=nil stop=stop tokens_in=17467 tokens_out=186
[2026-09-07 21:50:53] REQ 260907215043-8 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=16 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_208xehua","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"cross-response-repetition-guard"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:50:53] === description ===\nThe deepseek text-only loop repeats the SAME paragraph ACROSS responses (not within one). The output-runaway guard (20 identical lines in ONE response) misses it until the final 65536-token response, where the truncated-output check fires first. A cross-response guard tracking the most-repeated line across the last N responses would catch the loop at response ~5, saving ~24 responses of burn. c111 finding.\n\n=== design ===\n# Cross-Response Repetition Guard -- design (c111 finding)\n\n## The gap\n\nThe deepseek text-only loop repeats the SAME paragraph ACROSS responses,\nnot within one. The existing output-runaway guard\n(`iar--cycle-output-runaway-p`, 20 identical trimmed lines in ONE\nresponse) never fires on the loop's early responses -- each carries only\n5-10 repetitions (under threshold). The burn accumulates across\nresponses: the 21:10 cycle burned 22 requests / 471k input tokens /\n74k output before the FINAL response (16712 identical lines, 65536\ntokens, stop=length) where the truncated-output check fires FIRST in\nthe cond and ends the cycle.\n\nSo the per-response guard is the wrong granularity for this class. The\nloop's signature is: the same line/paragraph appears in MANY consecutive\nresponses, each under the per-response threshold.\n\n## Evidence (c111, cycle 21:10 UTC)\n\n- 22 requests, 471503 input tokens, 74163 output, deepseek-v4-flash.\n- Last response: 16712 identical \"Let me think about what I can actually\n  do this cycle...\" lines, 65536 tokens, stop=length.\n- Truncated-output guard fired (correctly) and ended the cycle.\n- Earlier responses each had 5-10 repetitions -- under the 20-line\n  per-response threshold, so the output-runaway guard never fired.\n\n## Design\n\nTrack the most-repeated trimmed line across the last N responses\n(N ~ 5). Maintain a hash table of line -> count, keyed by response\nboundary. When a line's cumulative count across the window exceeds a\nthreshold (e.g. 30), fire the same recovery path as the output-runaway\nguard (one recovery round-trip, then end on second fire).\n\nThis catches the loop at response ~5 instead of the final response,\nsaving ~17 requests of burn (~400k input tokens per occurrence).\n\n## Notes\n\n- The truncated-output check stays FIRST in the cond (it is the\n  stronger, cheaper signal when it fires).\n- The cross-response guard is a NEW check, not a replacement.\n- Thresholds need tuning against real data (the 21:10 cycle's early\n  responses had 5-10 reps; a window of 5 responses x 10 reps = 50\n  cumulative would fire around response 5-6).\n- Test: construct a synthetic multi-response sequence where each\n  response has 5-10 reps of the same line (under per-response\n  threshold) and assert the cross-response guard fires."}]
