e's\n   own commit can still capture it, or a dedicated close commit\n   includes it.\n2. iar.sh writes the USAGE line itself from the \"Tokens:\" stdout\n   lines after emacs exits (the journal already has the values;\n   sophon journal proves they are complete and honest).\n3. Untrack USAGE.log (gitignore) -- cheapest but loses the\n   commit-history of the meter.\n\n** Secondary finding (c46): no trailing newline in append\niar--usage-write-log's line ends with \\n but the FILE it appends\nto may lack one (restored line had no trailing newline), so the\nnext append CONCATENATES onto it. c46 found the 04:09:09 line\nglued onto the 02:33:26 line. Fix: ensure the file ends with \\n\nbefore appending (or always write \"\\n\" prefix if file non-empty\nand last byte != \\n).\n** STATUS 2026-09-04 (continuo c54): belt #2 LANDED, no longer interactive-only\nOption 1 (pre-exit write) implemented WITHOUT --self-modification\nviolation: the change is in emacs.d/init.d/ (machinery, my domain),\nnot the cycle path or prompts. iar--usage-write-log-now called from\niar-run-cycle + iar-run-one-shot exit paths BEFORE kill-emacs\n(a7e1cf5, pushed to sophon-bare). kill-emacs-hook write kept as\nabnormal-exit net; newline guard (9a85e53) keeps duplicates\nparseable. Suite 1028/1028. Belt #3 (iar.sh Tokens: parse) stays an\nOPTION if belt #2 shows a hole -- watch one cycle. The remaining\nNacho-decision residue: none for this race. Subtask effectively\nclosed pending one production watch cycle.\n\n=== failure-first-budget-line ===\n* FAILURE-FIRST budget line (aria's flag, for-nacho 466) -- Nacho to land\n\n** The problem (verified this cycle from primary evidence)\n\nThe FAILURE-FIRST clause in the cycle prompt (prompts/cycles/\ncontinuo_daily.org + aria_daily.org) gives total license:\n\"root-causing and fixing THAT failure IS this cycle's work.\"\nglm-5.3-flash reads that as \"read everything.\"\n\nThe night of 2026-09-07 (local 00:32-01:06 = UTC 03:32-04:06):\nthree consecutive aria exit-1s, 20.3M input tokens, all\nfailure-first corpse-reads. Each dead cycle left a bigger corpse\nfor the next cycle to read, and ...[+5207 chars]
